  "verdicts": [
    {
      "claim": "CoefLeg blocks reconstruct the dense experiment magnitude angular shape: mean affine R2 ~0.90-0.93 under reading B (order index = degree), only ~0.25 under reading A (family = fixed harmonic)",
      "reproduced": true,
      "my_value": "reading B: mean affine R2 = 0.9307 (best convention CS0_norm1_sq20), 0.9311 with the interpolated dense reference; range over the 8 convention combos 0.778-0.931. reading A: mean affine R2 = 0.2546 (best convention CS1_norm1_sq21), 0.2546 interpolated; range over conventions 0.127-0.255.",
      "method": "own associated-Legendre recurrence (no CS phase, verified against scipy.lpmv to 1e-15) + numpy.polyfit affine R2, 8-convention grid, dense reference taken both as nearest 0.1 eV panel and as linear interpolation of the bracketing panels",
      "comment": "Per-energy spread: reading B 0.884..0.979, reading A 0.005..0.535 (nearest reference), so the means match the claim but the per-energy scatter is large. affineR2 == corr^2 verified to 1e-12. Reading-B per-energy: [0.9199, 0.9791, 0.8845, 0.8987, 0.9302, 0.9128, 0.8999, 0.959, 0.9662, 0.9609, 0.9493, 0.9248, 0.9133]"
    },
    {
      "claim": "F00 at order index 0 is pinned to 1.0 +- 4e-5 across all 13 energies; F11 is exactly zero at order 0",
      "reproduced": true,
      "my_value": "max |F00(order0)-1| = 4.0000000000040004e-05 over the 13 energies (raw values ['1.00002', '1.00001', '1.00001', '1.00001', '1.00002', '1.00003', '1.00004', '1.00002', '1.00003', '1.00002', '1.00001', '1.00001', '1.0']); F11(order0) exactly 0.0 at all 13 energies: True",
      "method": "direct read of the angular_coefficients blocks (sort+reshape route, cross-checked entry-for-entry against pivot_table)",
      "comment": "The largest deviation comes from the 31.0 eV entry, stored as 1.0000399999999999 (2 ulp above 1.00004); it exceeds 4e-5 by 3.6e-21, i.e. a strict-float boundary artefact, so the claim reproduces at its stated precision. F11 is exactly 0.0 at order 0 in every energy and exactly 0.0 in orders 1..8 too (no nonzero F11 anywhere). Exact-zero pattern over all families: {\"F00\": {\"value_zero_orders_all13\": [], \"err_zero_orders_all13\": []}, \"F20\": {\"value_zero_orders_all13\": [], \"err_zero_orders_all13\": []}, \"F21\": {\"value_zero_orders_all13\": [0], \"err_zero_orders_all13\": [0]}, \"F22\": {\"value_zero_orders_all13\": [0, 1], \"err_zero_orders_all13\": [0, 1]}, \"F11\": {\"value_zero_orders_all13\": [0], \"err_zero_orders_all13\": [0]}}"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The F families are NOT predictable from the experiment DME blocks: in-sample full-dictionary R2 = 1.0 with rank 13 of 105 features; leave-one-out R2 for the best single feature <= 0.27 for F00 and negative for F20; permutation p >= 0.8 for the maximum single-feature correlation",
      "reproduced": true,
      "my_value": "in-sample full-dict R2 = 1.0000000000..1.0000000000 (rank of the 105-col design = 13 of 13 energies); greedy per-fold LOO R2: F00 1feat=0.2699 2feat=0.3440, F20 1feat=-0.2817 2feat=0.0671; LOO with the single feature fixed on the full data: F00=-0.0091, F20=0.3007; permutation p for the max |single-feature r|: F00 0.940 (117-label null) / 0.080 (13-energy-block null), F20 0.820 / 0.105; ridge LOO over the alpha path (12 training energies, so edf<=8 counts as non-interpolating) F00=0.7216, F20=0.7046",
      "method": "closed-form greedy LOO from centred Gram/cross-product matrices (no repeated lstsq); two permutation nulls (117-label shuffle and 13-energy-block shuffle); ridge LOO over an explicit alpha path with edf tracking; energy-only linear/cubic LOO baselines",
      "comment": "in-sample R2 is saturated because rank(DIC)=13=number of energies; the honest greedy LOO values are near zero or negative (F00 1feat=0.2699, F20 1feat=-0.2817 - the claim's 'best single feature' numbers; exact match to the package). The harsher energy-block (structure-preserving) permutation null gives F00 p=0.080 and F20 p=0.105, and its 95th pct of max|null r| is 0.111 (F00) / 0.154 (F20), so the max correlations are already inside that null. SHARPEST CAVEAT: a heavily-regularised ridge on the full 105-feature dictionary reaches genuine LOO R2 = 0.7216 (F00), 0.7046 (F20), 0.5455 (F21), 0.3820 (F22), 0.5552 (F11) at edf~8-11 of 12 - permutation p=0.000 against an energy-shuffled null - so the families ARE predictable in a genuine out-of-sample sense once pooling over the 9 order rows and shrinking 105 collinear features. That does not contradict the claim's literal statistics (best SINGLE feature and the rank-13 in-sample fit) but it does contradict its broad gloss 'NOT predictable from the experiment DME blocks'. Energy-only baselines (no DME): linear F00 -0.004, F20 -0.017; cubic -17.5/-22.7."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Reconstruction quality is stable between the 13-energy set and the 7 on-grid subset",
      "reproduced": true,
      "my_value": "max |mean(on-grid7) - mean(all13)| over the 8 conventions: reading B 0.0150, reading A 0.0163; reading B best convention all13=0.9307 on-grid7=0.9233 off-grid6=0.9392; 5000-draw permutation test for the on-grid vs off-grid mean-R2 difference: observed -0.0159, p=0.340",
      "method": "per-convention mean affine R2 on the 13/7/6 energy subsets plus a permutation test that relabels which 7 of the 13 energies are 'on-grid'",
      "comment": "The on-grid subset is not specially better or worse; the difference is within the permutation noise (p=0.340). reading B per convention: {\"CS0_norm0_sq20\": {\"all13\": 0.8512, \"ongrid7\": 0.8422, \"offgrid6\": 0.8617, \"diff\": -0.009}, \"CS0_norm0_sq21\": {\"all13\": 0.7778, \"ongrid7\": 0.7709, \"offgrid6\": 0.7858, \"diff\": -0.0069}, \"CS0_norm1_sq20\": {\"all13\": 0.9307, \"ongrid7\": 0.9233, \"offgrid6\": 0.9392, \"diff\": -0.0073}, \"CS0_norm1_sq21\": {\"all13\": 0.926, \"ongrid7\": 0.9193, \"offgrid6\": 0.9337, \"diff\": -0.0066}, \"CS1_norm0_sq20\": {\"all13\": 0.8561, \"ongrid7\": 0.8638, \"offgrid6\": 0.847, \"diff\": 0.0078}, \"CS1_norm0_sq21\": {\"all13\": 0.8039, \"ongrid7\": 0.8189, \"offgrid6\": 0.7864, \"diff\": 0.015}, \"CS1_norm1_sq20\": {\"all13\": 0.9078, \"ongrid7\": 0.9084, \"offgrid6\": 0.9071, \"diff\": 0.0006}, \"CS1_norm1_sq21\": {\"all13\": 0.8972, \"ongrid7\": 0.9005, \"offgrid6\": 0.8935, \"diff\": 0.0032}}"
    }
  ],
  "residual_doubt": "(1) Reading B is not convention-free: only the best of the 8 CS/normalisation/sqrt(2) combos reaches 0.90-0.93 (mean 0.9307); the worst combo gives 0.7778, so a different harmonic convention weakens the reconstruction. Reading A stays 0.13-0.25 for every convention, so the A-vs-B dichotomy itself is robust. (2) For the six off-grid energies the dense reference is a derived spline grid; nearest and interpolated references agree to <=0.002 in the mean, but that comparison is not fully independent. (3) Permutation p-values rest on 13 energies (200 draws for the max-r null, 5000 for claim 4). (4) Claim 2 is literally correct for the statistics it names, but my harsher ridge test (105 collinear features, edf~8-11 of 12 training energies) finds genuine out-of-sample LOO R2 of 0.72 (F00), 0.70 (F20), 0.55 (F21), 0.38 (F22), 0.56 (F11) with permutation p<=0.015, so the family values carry real information about the DME block when pooled over the 9 order rows; the 'NOT predictable' gloss is model-class dependent, and the per-energy ridge R2 is unstable (worst energy can be negative).",
